{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02817",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.29,
      "end_seconds": 6.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Morning, you know, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.29,
      "end_seconds": 11.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.58,
      "end_seconds": 19.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.22,
      "text": "Mainly I've been feeling lightheaded during an episode. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.36,
      "end_seconds": 23.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.91,
      "end_seconds": 29.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Well, I've had it since this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.7,
      "end_seconds": 40.64,
      "duration_seconds": 9.94,
      "text": "Okay, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.32,
      "end_seconds": 46.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "It happens on and off. Severe, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.29,
      "end_seconds": 51.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Okay, have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.14,
      "end_seconds": 64.48,
      "duration_seconds": 11.34,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a pounding in my neck as well. Oh, and my heart suddenly racing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.97,
      "end_seconds": 70.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "So, any it stopping just as suddenly as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.86,
      "end_seconds": 71.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Yes, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.79,
      "end_seconds": 78.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Have you been feeling lightheaded during an episode at any time before this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.51,
      "end_seconds": 85.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "A bit, last year. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.24,
      "end_seconds": 87.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.16,
      "end_seconds": 92.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.19,
      "end_seconds": 94.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.51,
      "end_seconds": 101.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.6,
      "end_seconds": 107.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.27,
      "end_seconds": 114.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.06,
      "end_seconds": 119.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.14,
      "end_seconds": 125.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.53,
      "end_seconds": 129.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.63,
      "end_seconds": 135.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.22,
      "end_seconds": 155.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.34,
      "end_seconds": 158.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Yes, eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.41,
      "end_seconds": 160.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Yes, carry on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.78,
      "end_seconds": 164.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Diabetes, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.07,
      "end_seconds": 173.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "Right, so diabetes is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.52,
      "end_seconds": 185.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.62,
      "text": "Hydrocortisone cream. I take it when needed. I, I take sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 185.66,
      "end_seconds": 191.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 50 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.13,
      "end_seconds": 195.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.21,
      "end_seconds": 201.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Ah, not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.25,
      "end_seconds": 218.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.91,
      "end_seconds": 223.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.31,
      "end_seconds": 229.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Have you noticed breathlessness, fainting or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.64,
      "end_seconds": 233.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.05,
      "end_seconds": 238.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "How about family history of sudden death?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.35,
      "end_seconds": 245.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "I, I haven't noticed any family history of sudden death."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.93,
      "end_seconds": 250.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.77,
      "end_seconds": 253.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.55,
      "end_seconds": 258.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.13,
      "end_seconds": 260.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 275.62,
      "end_seconds": 285.68,
      "duration_seconds": 10.06,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pulse 77, temperature is 36.5 degrees, oxygen saturation is 97 percent. BP is 119 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.57,
      "end_seconds": 288.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.76,
      "end_seconds": 292.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Alright, may I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.07,
      "end_seconds": 294.77,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.06,
      "end_seconds": 297.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.94,
      "end_seconds": 314.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Your heart sounds and rhythm are normal today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.25,
      "end_seconds": 330.94,
      "duration_seconds": 11.69,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Right, here's what I'm thinking. I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at episodes of supraventricular tachycardia or atrial fibrillation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 334.75,
      "end_seconds": 337.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "We've already done an ECG this morning, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.8,
      "end_seconds": 361.66,
      "duration_seconds": 21.86,
      "text": "Thanks, that helps. I think a 7-day heart monitor makes sense here, for paroxysmal palpitations. Try blowing hard against a closed mouth and nose when it starts. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.25,
      "end_seconds": 367.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Okay, so I know what to watch for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.7,
      "end_seconds": 375.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "Let's plan a check after the monitor. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.79,
      "end_seconds": 379.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}